% ================================================================
% 12 — approx. 40 s: Conclusion.
% ================================================================

To conclude, the main motivation behind this research is the problem of unwanted wave re-reflections in laboratory experiments.

When reflected waves return to the wavemaker and are reflected again, they interfere with the intended wave conditions and reduce the reliability of experimental measurements.

My thesis investigates whether a machine-learning-based controller can address this problem by adjusting the piston motion to absorb returning waves while preserving the incident waves.

The main contribution will be implementing this approach in OpenFOAM, a freely available and open-source CFD framework, and comparing its performance with conventional methods.

Through these comparisons, I aim to establish both the potential advantages and the limitations of machine-learning-based wave absorption.

